[ti:Day 30]

[00:00.00]customary 例 It is both customary and expected for customers to tip waiters when going out to restaurants, bars, and coffee shops in America. 在美国，当外出就餐、上酒吧、去咖啡 馆的时候，顾客最好能给服务生一些小费，这也 是一种惯例。
[00:17.99]appendix 例 For convenience, we have also provided a glossary in an appendix. 为了方便使用, 我们在 附录中也提供了术语表。
[00:27.83]automotive 例 Despite the obvious growing pains, working together is the best means of long-term success in the automotive industry. 尽管在早期 发展中困难很多，但通力合作是在汽车产业取得 长期成功的最佳方式。
[00:45.05]itemise 例 It is necessary to itemise a detailed and nationwide market access catalogue for private investment. 有必要列出一份全国范围内 的私人投资市场准入细则。
[00:59.50]paperwork 例 She is the right person for the paperwork. 她是文书工作的合适人选。
[01:06.42]standardise 例 We will take measures to standardise the procedure of legal services. 我们将采取措施， 规范法律服务程序。
[01:17.34]foodstuff 例 The government maintains strategic reserves of pork and salt among its major foodstuff resources. 政府一直对猪肉与盐这些主 要食品资源采取战略性储备措施。
[01:31.79]augment 例 If prices remain high, more of the world's existing stock will augment supply. 如果金价继 续维持高位，现有的储备将会增加供给。
[01:43.17]barcode 例 You can scan the barcode on an item and then can access the information of the product. 先扫描商品上的条形码，然后你就能查 看到关于该产品的信息。
[01:55.31]acquire 例 It is necessary to acquire a good knowledge of marketing. 掌握丰富的市场营销知 识非常必要。
[02:03.92]interface 例 The page interface is user-friendly and easy to operate. 该网页界面友好、操作方便。
[02:12.84]advance 例 She asked the company director for an advance on a month's salary. 她请求公司主管 预付自己一个月的薪水。
[02:22.53]lateral 例 There will be some lateral transfers for him in the company. 公司将会对他进行横向调动。
[02:31.45]fractious 例 The art of Belgian political leadership consists of bringing consensus to a broad and fractious coalition. 比利时的政治领导艺术在于 让一个难以驾驭的大联盟形成共识。
[02:46.98]exotic 例 Exotic vocabulary can often be heard in daily life due to globalisation. 随着全球化的发 展，日常生活中经常可以听到外来词。
[02:57.43]derive 例 The world economy failed to derive much support from the continued weakness of the dollar. 世界经济未能从持续萎靡的美元获得多少 支持。
[03:10.20]pivotal 例 She plays a pivotal role in product design. 她在产品设计工作中起着关键作用。
[03:16.96]cushion 例 Unfortunately it turned out that banks still wanted to hold excess reserves as a cushion. 不幸的是，银行仍旧想把超额储备金当做一种缓 冲继续握紧不放。
[03:29.72]furious 例 He gulped back the furious reply he wanted to make. 他强忍住了本想作出的愤怒回答。
[03:37.41]absorb 例 The firms usually absorb the higher wage costs by raising prices of their commodities. 公司通常通过提高商品价格来承担越来越高的薪 资开支。
[03:49.71]sprint 例 Speed is essential in a sprint. 速度在短跑中 极其重要。
[03:54.79]amusement 例 Outdoor amusement will help you relax after a day's work at the offlce. 在办公室里工 作了一整天之后，户外娱乐活动可使你得到放 松。
[04:05.39]allot 例 I allot a certain amount of time to analyse the historic data on stock each day. 我每天都 匀出一定的时间来分析股票交易历史数据。
[04:16.31]formulate 例 They must be qualifled to analyze, appraise and interpret economic data and government programs, as well as formulate and recommend national economic policy. 他们必 须能够分析、评价并解释经济数据和政府项目， 以及系统阐述和规划国家经济政策。
[04:38.61]noncommittal 例 With regard to labour insurance，the Union President gave a noncommittal answer. 关于劳 动保险，工会主席没有给出明确的回答。
[04:51.21]fluffy 例 It's a very fluffy kind of wool. 这种羊毛质地 非常柔软。
[04:56.29]acute 例 The economic crisis in Europe has moved from an acute phase to a chronic one. 欧洲的 经济危机已由爆发阶段转入持续阶段。
[05:06.90]monopolise 例 Our company has monopolised the mobile market for so many decades that we don't worry about competition f rom other companies. 我们公司已经垄断手机市场数十年， 来自其他公司的竞争不会给我们造成困扰。
[05:24.89]fiscal 例 The accountants will audit the company's books at the end of the flscal year. 财年结束 时，会计师们会审查公司的账目。
[05:35.80]despatch 例 The despatch of railway transportation must be unifled and the construction of the overall network must be under integrated planning. 铁路运输的发送必须统一，而且整个网 络建设必须整体规划。
[05:54.72]deadlock 例 Gold prices in China declined in December as the deadlock in the United States' fiscal cliff bargain added to the market uncertainty. 由于美国“财政悬崖”交易的僵局加大了市场的不 确定性，中国的黄金价格在12月份下降了。
[06:13.32]malign 例 You malign a hard-working employee when you call him a lazy person. 你说这样一位努力工 作的员工懒散，这是对他的恶意诽谤。
[06:23.01]flawed 例 From my experience, at least 2/3 of all business plans we received are flawed. 根据我 的经验，我们收到的商业计划中至少有2/3是有缺 陷的。
[06:34.08]politicise 例 He raised objections at efforts to politicise the national army. 他反对将国家军队政治化。
[06:44.23]fling 例 You shouldn't fling away a chance like that. 你不该让这么一个机会随意溜走。
[06:50.84]doldrums 例 Affected by the global financial crisis, America remains in the economic doldrums. 受 全球金融危机的影响，美国的经济仍然停滞不 前。
[07:03.14]faulty 例 To achieve the objective, we would change the former faulty understanding of development. 为了实现这一目标，我们将改变之 前对发展的错误理解。
[07:16.06]divisive 例 She believes that unemployment is socially divisive and is leading to the creation of an underclass. 他认为失业会造成社会分化，并会导 致贫困阶层的产生。
[07:30.51]workaholic 例 She really lives up to the reputation as a workaholic. 她是个名副其实的工作狂。
[07:39.12]retrench 例 Two hundred workers were retrenched during the flnancial crisis. 在这次金融危机中， 有200名员工被裁掉。
[07:49.11]commonplace 例 A $99 extension of a commonplace device will be a no-brainer for a large set of media consumers. 一个99美元的普通扩展设备对于大 量的媒体消费者而言稀松平常。 search engine 搜索引擎 cope with 处理，对付，应付 例 These remedies are never perfect, so ultimately you must cope with the variations. 这些补救措施永远不会完美，所以最终必须由你 来处理偏差。
[08:03.11]hotbed 例 As a hotbed of war, these islands are home to many sunken freighters, submarines and planes. 作为战争的温床，这些岛屿拥有很多沉没 的货轮、潜艇和飞机。
[08:16.02]correspond 例 His design, for the most part, corresponds with the actual needs. 他的设计在很大程度上符 合实际需要。
[08:26.17]proliferation 例 No one can stop mobile device proliferation. 任何人都无法阻止移动设备的不断 推广。
[08:34.16]freelance 例 Finding freelance work can be tough, especially if you're just getting into the industry. 找到一份自由职业者的工作是很难的， 尤其在刚入行的时候。
[08:47.39]launch 例 The company advocates all the salesmen to launch a big promotion for their new products. 公司号召全体销售人员为其新产品发起一场大型 的促销活动。
[08:59.84]accredit 例 He is accredited as being the flrst person to bring in the new concept of cost control. 他 被公认为是第一个引进成本控制新理念的人。
[09:12.14]haemorrhage 例 On further examination the true reason why the company haemorrhaged money for months will be found. 通过进一步的调查，数月来公司流 失大量资金的原因就会水落石出。
[09:26.90]heighten 例 The advertising company is constantly looking for new techniques to heighten its surveillance of Internet users. 这家广告公司不 断寻求新技术，以加强对互联网用户的行为监 测。
[09:43.20]outskirts 例 The store is situated in the outskirts of the small town. 那家商店位于小镇的郊区。
[09:51.97]vacant 例 The post of general manager fell vacant following his resignation. 总经理辞职之后，他 的职位就空缺着。
[10:01.81]retrain 例 She is currently retraining to become a real lawyer. 为了成为一名真正的律师，她正在复修课 程。
[10:09.80]revalue 例 Such issues can provide new common ground between the US and Japan. 这样的问题 可以为美日两国提供新的共同基础。
[10:19.64]invitation 例 We have received your invitation for Bid No. 315. 兹收到贵公司寄来的315号招标单。
[10:27.64]wane 例 Some traditional sections are beginning to wane amid soaring labour costs and outdated business models. 在激增的劳动力成本和过时的
[10:42.09]tighten 例 Money has started to tighten due to the flnancial crisis. 由于金融危机，银根开始紧缩。
[10:50.70]economise 例 Robots are used in some factories to economise on the cost of manpower. 为了节约 劳动力成本，一些厂家使用了机器人。
